WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.789
Each runbook step leaves a record
the security officer keeps,

2
00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:07.162
mapped to NIST's controls in
the kit's requirements file.

3
00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:11.274
The preflight supports least
privilege and configuration settings.

4
00:00:11.274 --> 00:00:15.700
The plan supports configuration
change control and impact analysis.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.550
The rollback supports change
control and the contingency plan.

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.988
Each scheduled run supports
continuous monitoring,

7
00:00:22.988 --> 00:00:26.425
the component inventory and
each area's own controls.

8
00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:30.775
The comparison supports configuration
settings and continuous monitoring.

9
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:33.365
And the chain of records
supports continuous

10
00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:36.363
monitoring and the protection
of audit information.

11
00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:40.275
The evidence supports those
controls; the assessor decides.

12
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:44.838
The key security indicators are
FedRAMP's indicators for cloud providers,

13
00:00:44.838 --> 00:00:48.860
which the agency lines its own
evidence up with and doesn't report.
